* The iterate of a function at a sum of exponents: the outer iterate applied to the inner one.  The step-counting engine of the machine layer.

s1::simp1l |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> B e. V )
s2::simp1r |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> G : B --> B )
s3::simp2l |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> N e. NN0 )
s4::simp2r |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> M e. NN0 )
s5::simp3 |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> X e. B )
i6::fex
s7:s2,s1,i6:syl2anc |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> G e. _V )
i8::ffun
s9:s2,i8:syl |- ( ( ( B e. V /\ G : B --> B ) /\ ( N e. NN0 /\ M e. NN0 ) /\ X e. B ) -> Fun G )
